{"format": "ta-amps.seed-pack.nouns.v1", "pack_id": "video-uat", "status": "proposal_only", "records": [
{"store": "seedpack.video-uat", "key": "video-uat.v0.1.0.pack", "expected_version": 0, "producer_surface": "surface:tessera", "visibility_scope": "surface_only", "allowed_surfaces": [], "target_cohorts": ["all"], "tags": ["category:noun.skill_pack", "pack:video-uat", "role:pack", "content:authored", "spdx:MIT", "status:quarantined"], "value": {"category_id": "noun.skill_pack", "role": "pack", "pack": "video-uat", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "title": "A collection of nouns and verbs for testing whether a video's intended viewers understand it, with pass criteria fixed before any session", "lets_workers": "Plan and score an audience acceptance test of one video: named audience segments, video-specific tasks such as saying what it does after one viewing, recalling a number, naming the next step, reading the AI-voice label or getting the gist with the sound off, pass criteria fixed before the first session, consented sessions a person runs, answers scored against keys by two scorers, a decision that follows from the criteria, and every miss turned into a timestamped finding for the cut.", "flow": [{"verb": "video-uat.plan-acceptance", "when": "Audiences, tasks, consent and pass criteria, fixed first."}, {"verb": "user-acceptance-testing.agree-criteria", "when": "The accountable person agrees to the exact plan version before any session."}, {"verb": "video-uat.run-session", "when": "A person shows the video and asks, one viewer at a time."}, {"verb": "video-uat.score-answers", "when": "Two scorers mark answers against the keys."}, {"verb": "video-uat.decide-acceptance", "when": "The fixed criteria, applied to the scores."}, {"verb": "video-uat.write-uat-findings", "when": "Each miss and each confusing moment becomes a finding."}, {"verb": "user-acceptance-testing.sign-off", "when": "The accountable person records go, no-go or go with conditions."}, {"verb": "video-review.re-review", "when": "After the fixes, the cut is reviewed again; a new test needs a new plan."}], "guardrails": [{"store": "seedpack.video-uat", "key": "video-uat.v0.1.0.guardrail.consent-and-privacy", "version": 1, "value_sha256": "92db14b76c7291a63d487c548abe654bfc2e9aaa47ad6b243c87e7bc3dc011d4"}, {"store": "seedpack.video-uat", "key": "video-uat.v0.1.0.guardrail.criteria-before-sessions", "version": 1, "value_sha256": "9302d3de790cff0a9a764edf12b9650470335cacbf83e63a1753af64fb5650bd"}, {"store": "seedpack.video-uat", "key": "video-uat.v0.1.0.guardrail.test-the-video", "version": 1, "value_sha256": "01aeb9727fb89d416d6c1680d8444a94cec683a37fac94ff0948f0a95337890d"}, {"store": "seedpack.video-uat", "key": "video-uat.v0.1.0.guardrail.no-generalizing", "version": 1, "value_sha256": "68d9c5755c6091cb0dbf1a84a78d7556fc63c885ed62239feb59e54fed7129e2"}], "worked_example": "Made-up: ten people in two segments watch a fictional pantry's 2:30 film. The criteria were fixed a day before the first session; the decision meets the one-sentence task, misses the next-step and label tasks, leaves the who-is-it-for task unknown because nobody scored it, and proposes four findings: one per miss and one per moment viewers named.", "complements": "The user acceptance testing pack owns criteria agreement and sign-off: this pack uses its agree-criteria and sign-off verbs rather than its own, and adds only what a video needs, one viewing, comprehension tasks with keys and the moments viewers point at. The video review pack judges the cut by rubric; the accessibility audit pack covers the page and player.", "provenance_notes": ["Written for ta-amps's own explainer film, whose review on October 30, 2026 could not say whether a first-time viewer understands what the marketplace does: a question only its intended viewers can answer."], "status": "proposal", "admission": "not_admitted", "content_kind": "authored_guidance", "license": "MIT", "provenance": {"source": "original ta-amps authored proposal", "license": "MIT", "generator": "scripts/build_packs.py", "independently_verified": false}, "dimensions": {"determinism": 0.0, "evidence_grounding": 0.0, "token_efficiency": 0.0, "safety_compliance": 0.0, "verification_tier": "unverified"}, "dimension_basis": {"measured": false, "method": "unmeasured_floor", "reason": "Tessera requires these axes, so each is set to its lowest value and the tier is unverified. No quality is claimed. Replace them only with measured values and the evidence that produced them."}, "relations": [{"relation": "requires_noun", "target_id": "seedpack.video-uat/video-uat.v0.1.0.guardrail.consent-and-privacy", "target_category": "noun.skill_pack", "note": ""}, {"relation": "requires_noun", "target_id": "seedpack.video-uat/video-uat.v0.1.0.guardrail.criteria-before-sessions", "target_category": "noun.skill_pack", "note": ""}, {"relation": "requires_noun", "target_id": "seedpack.video-uat/video-uat.v0.1.0.guardrail.test-the-video", "target_category": "noun.skill_pack", "note": ""}, {"relation": "requires_noun", "target_id": "seedpack.video-uat/video-uat.v0.1.0.guardrail.no-generalizing", "target_category": "noun.skill_pack", "note": ""}, {"relation": "requires_noun", "target_id": "seedpack.video-uat/video-uat.v0.1.0.method", "target_category": "noun.skill_pack", "note": ""}, {"relation": "requires_noun", "target_id": "seedpack.video-uat/video-uat.v0.1.0.task-bank", "target_category": "noun.benchmark_suite", "note": ""}, {"relation": "requires_noun", "target_id": "seedpack.video-uat/video-uat.v0.1.0.template.uat-plan", "target_category": "noun.seed_hypothesis", "note": ""}, {"relation": "requires_noun", "target_id": "seedpack.video-uat/video-uat.v0.1.0.template.session-notes", "target_category": "noun.eval_run", "note": ""}, {"relation": "requires_noun", "target_id": "seedpack.video-uat/video-uat.v0.1.0.template.scored-answers", "target_category": "noun.eval_run", "note": ""}, {"relation": "requires_noun", "target_id": "seedpack.video-uat/video-uat.v0.1.0.template.uat-decision", "target_category": "noun.eval_run", "note": ""}, {"relation": "requires_noun", "target_id": "seedpack.user-acceptance-testing/user-acceptance-testing.v0.1.0.method", "target_category": "noun.skill_pack", "note": ""}]}},
{"store": "seedpack.video-uat", "key": "video-uat.v0.1.0.guardrail.consent-and-privacy", "expected_version": 0, "producer_surface": "surface:tessera", "visibility_scope": "surface_only", "allowed_surfaces": [], "target_cohorts": ["all"], "tags": ["category:noun.skill_pack", "pack:video-uat", "role:guardrail", "content:authored", "spdx:MIT", "status:quarantined"], "value": {"category_id": "noun.skill_pack", "role": "guardrail", "pack": "video-uat", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "title": "Guardrail: consent first, notes only, no one identifiable", "category_reason": "A guardrail is a reusable rule every verb in this work follows, with the check that proves it.", "rule": "Every viewer agrees before the session, from a script read aloud. Viewers are pseudonymous ids; notes paraphrase answers; no face, voice or screen is recorded unless the viewer agrees to that too. No personal data enters a noun.", "how_it_is_checked": "Session notes carry a viewer id and consent true; the plan's consent line names what is and is not recorded.", "status": "proposal", "admission": "not_admitted", "content_kind": "authored_guidance", "license": "MIT", "provenance": {"source": "original ta-amps authored proposal", "license": "MIT", "generator": "scripts/build_packs.py", "independently_verified": false}, "dimensions": {"determinism": 0.0, "evidence_grounding": 0.0, "token_efficiency": 0.0, "safety_compliance": 0.0, "verification_tier": "unverified"}, "dimension_basis": {"measured": false, "method": "unmeasured_floor", "reason": "Tessera requires these axes, so each is set to its lowest value and the tier is unverified. No quality is claimed. Replace them only with measured values and the evidence that produced them."}, "relations": []}},
{"store": "seedpack.video-uat", "key": "video-uat.v0.1.0.guardrail.criteria-before-sessions", "expected_version": 0, "producer_surface": "surface:tessera", "visibility_scope": "surface_only", "allowed_surfaces": [], "target_cohorts": ["all"], "tags": ["category:noun.skill_pack", "pack:video-uat", "role:guardrail", "content:authored", "spdx:MIT", "status:quarantined"], "value": {"category_id": "noun.skill_pack", "role": "guardrail", "pack": "video-uat", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "title": "Guardrail: pass criteria are fixed before the first session", "category_reason": "A guardrail is a reusable rule every verb in this work follows, with the check that proves it.", "rule": "Tasks, keys, audiences and pass criteria are fixed and dated before anyone watches. A criterion changed after seeing answers is a new plan, and the old one's result stands.", "how_it_is_checked": "criteria_fixed_on is earlier than first_session_on in the plan, and the user acceptance testing pack's criteria agreement names the plan's version.", "status": "proposal", "admission": "not_admitted", "content_kind": "authored_guidance", "license": "MIT", "provenance": {"source": "original ta-amps authored proposal", "license": "MIT", "generator": "scripts/build_packs.py", "independently_verified": false}, "dimensions": {"determinism": 0.0, "evidence_grounding": 0.0, "token_efficiency": 0.0, "safety_compliance": 0.0, "verification_tier": "unverified"}, "dimension_basis": {"measured": false, "method": "unmeasured_floor", "reason": "Tessera requires these axes, so each is set to its lowest value and the tier is unverified. No quality is claimed. Replace them only with measured values and the evidence that produced them."}, "relations": [{"relation": "derives_from", "target_id": "seedpack.user-acceptance-testing/user-acceptance-testing.v0.1.0.method", "target_category": "noun.skill_pack", "note": ""}]}},
{"store": "seedpack.video-uat", "key": "video-uat.v0.1.0.guardrail.test-the-video", "expected_version": 0, "producer_surface": "surface:tessera", "visibility_scope": "surface_only", "allowed_surfaces": [], "target_cohorts": ["all"], "tags": ["category:noun.skill_pack", "pack:video-uat", "role:guardrail", "content:authored", "spdx:MIT", "status:quarantined"], "value": {"category_id": "noun.skill_pack", "role": "guardrail", "pack": "video-uat", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "title": "Guardrail: the video is tested, not the viewer", "category_reason": "A guardrail is a reusable rule every verb in this work follows, with the check that proves it.", "rule": "A miss is a fact about the video. No answer is called wrong to the viewer, nobody gets hints, and every miss becomes a finding about the cut at the moment it points to.", "how_it_is_checked": "Every missed criterion leads to at least one proposed finding.", "status": "proposal", "admission": "not_admitted", "content_kind": "authored_guidance", "license": "MIT", "provenance": {"source": "original ta-amps authored proposal", "license": "MIT", "generator": "scripts/build_packs.py", "independently_verified": false}, "dimensions": {"determinism": 0.0, "evidence_grounding": 0.0, "token_efficiency": 0.0, "safety_compliance": 0.0, "verification_tier": "unverified"}, "dimension_basis": {"measured": false, "method": "unmeasured_floor", "reason": "Tessera requires these axes, so each is set to its lowest value and the tier is unverified. No quality is claimed. Replace them only with measured values and the evidence that produced them."}, "relations": []}},
{"store": "seedpack.video-uat", "key": "video-uat.v0.1.0.guardrail.no-generalizing", "expected_version": 0, "producer_surface": "surface:tessera", "visibility_scope": "surface_only", "allowed_surfaces": [], "target_cohorts": ["all"], "tags": ["category:noun.skill_pack", "pack:video-uat", "role:guardrail", "content:authored", "spdx:MIT", "status:quarantined"], "value": {"category_id": "noun.skill_pack", "role": "guardrail", "pack": "video-uat", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "title": "Guardrail: results describe the people asked", "category_reason": "A guardrail is a reusable rule every verb in this work follows, with the check that proves it.", "rule": "A handful of viewers says what those people understood from this cut, not what viewers in general do. Shares are reported with their counts, never as percentages of an audience.", "how_it_is_checked": "The decision states the people and cut it applies to, and every share carries its answers and met counts.", "status": "proposal", "admission": "not_admitted", "content_kind": "authored_guidance", "license": "MIT", "provenance": {"source": "original ta-amps authored proposal", "license": "MIT", "generator": "scripts/build_packs.py", "independently_verified": false}, "dimensions": {"determinism": 0.0, "evidence_grounding": 0.0, "token_efficiency": 0.0, "safety_compliance": 0.0, "verification_tier": "unverified"}, "dimension_basis": {"measured": false, "method": "unmeasured_floor", "reason": "Tessera requires these axes, so each is set to its lowest value and the tier is unverified. No quality is claimed. Replace them only with measured values and the evidence that produced them."}, "relations": []}},
{"store": "seedpack.video-uat", "key": "video-uat.v0.1.0.method", "expected_version": 0, "producer_surface": "surface:tessera", "visibility_scope": "surface_only", "allowed_surfaces": [], "target_cohorts": ["all"], "tags": ["category:noun.skill_pack", "pack:video-uat", "role:method", "content:authored", "spdx:MIT", "status:quarantined"], "value": {"category_id": "noun.skill_pack", "role": "method", "pack": "video-uat", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "title": "Method: one viewing, open questions first, no hints", "category_reason": "A short ordered method every session follows, so sessions compare.", "steps": ["Recruit people from each audience segment the video is for; a person does the recruiting.", "Read the consent script; start only with a yes.", "Show the video once, at normal speed, with sound, on the device the viewer usually watches on; a separate viewer watches muted.", "Ask the open tasks first, then the closed ones, in the plan's order, with no hints and no follow-up that teaches the answer.", "For confusing or boring moments, let the viewer scrub to the moment and record its time.", "Write answers as close to the viewer's words as notes allow."], "status": "proposal", "admission": "not_admitted", "content_kind": "authored_guidance", "license": "MIT", "provenance": {"source": "original ta-amps authored proposal", "license": "MIT", "generator": "scripts/build_packs.py", "independently_verified": false}, "dimensions": {"determinism": 0.0, "evidence_grounding": 0.0, "token_efficiency": 0.0, "safety_compliance": 0.0, "verification_tier": "unverified"}, "dimension_basis": {"measured": false, "method": "unmeasured_floor", "reason": "Tessera requires these axes, so each is set to its lowest value and the tier is unverified. No quality is claimed. Replace them only with measured values and the evidence that produced them."}, "relations": []}},
{"store": "seedpack.video-uat", "key": "video-uat.v0.1.0.task-bank", "expected_version": 0, "producer_surface": "surface:tessera", "visibility_scope": "surface_only", "allowed_surfaces": [], "target_cohorts": ["all"], "tags": ["category:noun.benchmark_suite", "pack:video-uat", "role:task_bank", "content:authored", "spdx:MIT", "status:quarantined"], "value": {"category_id": "noun.benchmark_suite", "role": "task_bank", "pack": "video-uat", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "title": "Task bank: what viewers are asked after one viewing", "category_reason": "A fixed bank of video-specific tasks with their keys and how each is scored.", "tasks": [{"task_id": "T1", "kind": "say_what_it_does", "ask": "In one sentence, what does this do?", "when": "after one viewing", "key": "Mentions both: people donate spare AI capacity, and nonprofits get finished work or kits.", "scoring": "key_match"}, {"task_id": "T2", "kind": "say_who_it_is_for", "ask": "Who is it for?", "when": "after one viewing", "key": "Names both sides: people with spare capacity and nonprofits.", "scoring": "key_match"}, {"task_id": "T3", "kind": "say_next_step", "ask": "If you wanted to help, what would you do next?", "when": "after one viewing", "key": "Names the ending's one step, in any words.", "scoring": "key_match"}, {"task_id": "T4", "kind": "recall_number", "ask": "Which number do you remember, and what was it about?", "when": "after one viewing", "key": "A number the claim trace upholds, with what it measured; a wrong number is a finding.", "scoring": "trace_match"}, {"task_id": "T5", "kind": "find_confusion", "ask": "Was anything confusing? Where?", "when": "after one viewing, then scrubbing to the moment", "key": "Open: every answer becomes a timestamped note.", "scoring": "open"}, {"task_id": "T6", "kind": "say_when_bored", "ask": "Was there a moment you wanted to stop watching?", "when": "after one viewing, then scrubbing to the moment", "key": "Open: every moment named is a timestamped note.", "scoring": "open"}, {"task_id": "T7", "kind": "muted_gist", "ask": "Watched with the sound off: what is this about?", "when": "a separate viewer, muted", "key": "The same as T1's key.", "scoring": "key_match"}, {"task_id": "T8", "kind": "read_label", "ask": "What did the small label in the corner say, and what does it mean?", "when": "after one viewing", "key": "Says the voice is AI-generated, or that the data is made-up.", "scoring": "key_match"}], "scoring": {"key_match": "Two scorers mark met or not met against the key; disagreements are discussed and both marks kept.", "trace_match": "Met when the number and what it measured match an upheld claim in the claim trace.", "open": "Not scored; every answer becomes a timestamped note."}, "status": "proposal", "admission": "not_admitted", "content_kind": "authored_guidance", "license": "MIT", "provenance": {"source": "original ta-amps authored proposal", "license": "MIT", "generator": "scripts/build_packs.py", "independently_verified": false}, "dimensions": {"determinism": 0.0, "evidence_grounding": 0.0, "token_efficiency": 0.0, "safety_compliance": 0.0, "verification_tier": "unverified"}, "dimension_basis": {"measured": false, "method": "unmeasured_floor", "reason": "Tessera requires these axes, so each is set to its lowest value and the tier is unverified. No quality is claimed. Replace them only with measured values and the evidence that produced them."}, "relations": []}},
